app "gemblade" {
  // Match-3 with a sword arm, in pixel art. A knight fights one monster at a time, and every gem
  // swapped into a line of three or more does something: red blades and skulls strike the monster,
  // shields add armor, hearts heal, stars fill the mana for three spells, coins pay for the camp
  // between fights. The monster counts down and hits back every few moves. Ten foes to a round,
  // each worse than the last and a dragon at the end, and then they come round again, harder.
  //
  // There's no game loop: a swap resolves at once, cascades and all, in `on resN`, which leaves
  // what the board did in `steps` and the rest in timed events (`fx`, in seconds from `fxAt`, the
  // frame clock when the move began) for the canvases to play. Swaps (`on swN`) and spells
  // (`on spN`) set up `pend`, the board to resolve, and what happens before it.

  meta { owl: 12; description: "Match-3 with a sword arm, in pixel art: swap gems to strike monsters, raise armor, heal and charge spells; ten foes and a dragon, a camp between fights, then round again"; version: "1.0"; license: "MIT"; category: "games" }

  title: ""
  statusBar: false
  edge: true
